# Tracer: forall conclusions require one flat parameter header.
#
# Before (the removed preview syntax was accepted and normalized):
# forall x R:
#     x > 0
#     =>:
#         forall y R:
#             y > 0
#             =>:
#                 x + y > 0
# Former behavior: the parser rewrote this as one forall over x and y.
#
# Now (verified):
forall x, y R:
    x > 0
    y > 0
    =>:
        x + y > 0
# Current behavior: every quantified parameter is declared in one forall header.
#
# Boundary: the commented nested form is rejected by the executable parser regression
# block_forall_then_rejects_nested_forall in src/parse/parse_fact.rs.
# Evidence: this flat tracer verifies, and the named parser regression rejects the
# corresponding nested spelling.
# Implementation: src/parse/parse_fact.rs and src/fact/forall_fact.rs
